Package: tidyweave
Title: Composable R Workflows for Governed Data Products
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: person("Jan-Hendrik", "Weinert", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "65009403+JanWein@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Composes data acquisition, transformation, contracts and quality
    checks through simple R verbs and interchangeable S3 adapters. Runs ordinary
    data-frame workflows without infrastructure and optionally publishes immutable
    releases through DuckDB or DuckLake. Generates execution metadata and supports
    DBI sources, pointblank checks, dbt workflows, governed metrics and reports.
    Existing lazy database pipelines remain available for larger workloads.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: DBI, dplyr (>= 1.1.0), dbplyr, tibble, rlang, digest, jsonlite, methods
Suggests: duckdb (>= 1.5.5), testthat (>= 3.0.0), pointblank, dm, shiny, bslib, yaml,
    readr, readxl, paws.storage, knitr, rmarkdown, processx, withr,
    arrow, pins (>= 1.2.0), httr2, targets, renv, RSQLite, webfakes, bit64
Config/testthat/edition: 3
